<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<usx version="3.1">
<book code="MAL" style="id">BLB-Draft</book>

<para style="h">Malachi</para>

<para style="toc1">Malachi</para>

<para style="rem">sourceUrl=https://literalbible.com/blb.docx fetchedAtUtc=2026-09-01T15:43:00Z status=draft id=BLB-Draft spec=USFM-USX 3.1.1 char:add=docx-italic note:f=docx-footnotes note:x=docx-heading-crossrefs</para>

<chapter number="1" style="c" sid="MAL 1"/>

<para style="s">Yahweh’s Love for Israel</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="MAL 1:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Romans 9:6–29</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Genesis 25:19–28</char></note>The burden of the word of YHWH to Israel by the hand of Malachi:<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Malachi</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">My messenger</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> <verse eid="MAL 1:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="MAL 1:2"/>“I have loved you⁺,” says YHWH. </para>

<para style="p" vid="MAL 1:2">And you⁺ say, “In what way have You loved us?” “Was not Esau a brother to Jacob?” An utterance of YHWH. “And I have loved Jacob, <verse eid="MAL 1:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="MAL 1:3"/>and Esau I have hated, and I set his mountains <char style="add">as</char> a desolation and his inheritance for the jackals of the desert.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Romans 9:13</char></note>” <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to the serpents of the wilderness</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to the dragons of the wilderness</char></note><verse eid="MAL 1:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="MAL 1:4"/>If Edom should say, “We have been beaten down, and we will return and will build the ruins,” thus says YHWH of Hosts: “They may build, and I, I will tear down; and they will call to them the Territory of Wickedness, The people with whom YHWH will be angry even to forever. <verse eid="MAL 1:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="MAL 1:5"/>And your⁺ eyes will see, and you⁺ will say, ‘Great is YHWH from beyond the border of Israel!’” <verse eid="MAL 1:5"/></para>

<para style="s">The Polluted Offerings</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="MAL 1:6"/>“A son honors <char style="add">his</char> father, and a servant his master. And if I <char style="add">am</char> the Father, where is My honor? And if I <char style="add">am</char> the Master, where <char style="add">is</char> the fear due Me?” Says YHWH of Hosts to you⁺, O priests despising My name. </para>

<para style="p" vid="MAL 1:6">“And you⁺ say, ‘In what have we despised Your name?’ <verse eid="MAL 1:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="MAL 1:7"/>By bringing near upon My altar food <char style="add">that is</char> defiled. </para>

<para style="p" vid="MAL 1:7">And you⁺ say, ‘In what way have we defiled You?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">defiled it</char></note>’ </para>

<para style="p" vid="MAL 1:7">By your⁺ saying <char style="add">that</char> the table of YHWH, it is despised! <verse eid="MAL 1:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="MAL 1:8"/>For when you⁺ offer the blind as a sacrifice, <char style="add">is it</char> not evil? And when you⁺ offer the lame and sick, <char style="add">is it</char> not evil? Offer it now to your governor! Would he be pleased with you or would he lift up your face?” Says YHWH of Hosts. <verse eid="MAL 1:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="MAL 1:9"/>“And now, beseech, please, the face of God, and He will be gracious to us. From your⁺ hand this has come; will he lift up your⁺ faces?” Says YHWH of Hosts. <verse eid="MAL 1:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="MAL 1:10"/>“Who even among you⁺ will shut the doors, so that you⁺ could not kindle fire <char style="add">on</char> My altar in vain? There is not for Me delight in you⁺,” says YHWH of Hosts, “And an offering I will not accept from your⁺ hand! <verse eid="MAL 1:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="MAL 1:11"/>For from the rising of the sun to its going down, great <char style="add">is</char> My name among the nations; in every place incense shall be offered to My name, and a pure offering. Indeed, My name will be great among the nations.” Says YHWH of Hosts. <verse eid="MAL 1:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="MAL 1:12"/>“And you⁺ profane it by your⁺ saying, The table of the Lord, it is defiled,’ and of its fruit, ‘Its food is contemptible’ <verse eid="MAL 1:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="MAL 1:13"/>and You⁺ also say, ‘Behold, a weariness,’ and you⁺ sneer at it,” says YHWH of Hosts, </para>

<para style="p" vid="MAL 1:13">“And you⁺ bring the stolen, and the lame, and the sick, and you⁺ bring the offering! Should I accept this from your⁺ hands?” Says YHWH. <verse eid="MAL 1:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="MAL 1:14"/>“And cursed <char style="add">is</char> the one plotting, and a male is in his flock, and vowing <char style="add">it</char> and sacrificing <char style="add">what</char> is blemished to the Lord. For I <char style="add">am</char> a great King,” says YHWH of Hosts, “And My name is feared among the nations. <verse eid="MAL 1:14"/></para>

<chapter eid="MAL 1"/>

<chapter number="2" style="c" sid="MAL 2"/>

<para style="s">A Warning to the Priests</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="MAL 2:1"/><char style="add">“</char> And now, to you⁺ <char style="add">is</char> this commandment, O priests: <verse eid="MAL 2:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="MAL 2:2"/>If you⁺ do not listen and if you⁺ do not set <char style="add">it</char> upon the heart to give glory to My name,” says YHWH of Hosts, “Then I will send upon you⁺ the curse, and I will curse your⁺ blessings; indeed already I have cursed them, because there is none of you⁺ setting <char style="add">it</char> upon the heart. <verse eid="MAL 2:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="MAL 2:3"/>Behold, I am giving a rebuke to your⁺ seed,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">I am blighting your grain</char></note> and I will spread dung on your⁺ faces, the dung from your⁺ feasts, and it will carry you⁺ off with it. <verse eid="MAL 2:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="MAL 2:4"/>And you⁺ will know that I have sent to you⁺ this commandment, in order to continue My covenant with Levi,” says YHWH of Hosts. <verse eid="MAL 2:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="MAL 2:5"/>“My covenant was with him—life and peace—and I gave them to him; fear, and he feared Me, and before My name he was in awe. <verse eid="MAL 2:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="MAL 2:6"/>The law of truth was in his mouth, and injustice was not found on his lips; in peace and in uprightness He walked with Me, and many did he turn away from iniquity. <verse eid="MAL 2:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="MAL 2:7"/>For the lips of a priest should guard knowledge, and instruction they should seek from his mouth, for he <char style="add">is</char> the messenger of YHWH of Hosts. <verse eid="MAL 2:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="MAL 2:8"/>And you⁺ have turned aside from the way, you⁺ have caused many to stumble by <char style="add">your</char> instruction; you⁺ have corrupted the covenant of Levi,” says YHWH of Hosts. <verse eid="MAL 2:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="MAL 2:9"/>“And also I have made you⁺ despised and low before all the people, according to the measure by which you⁺ were not keeping guard of My ways, and were lifting faces regarding the instruction.” <verse eid="MAL 2:9"/></para>

<para style="s">Judah’s Unfaithfulness</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="MAL 2:10"/>Is there not for all of us one Father? Has not one God created us? Why do we act treacherously, a man against his brother, to profane the covenant of our fathers? <verse eid="MAL 2:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="MAL 2:11"/>Judah has acted treacherously, and an abomination has been done in Israel and in Jerusalem; for Judah has profaned the sanctuary of YHWH, which He loves, and he has married the daughter of a foreign god. <verse eid="MAL 2:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="MAL 2:12"/>May YHWH cut off the man who does this, the one being awake and the one answering from the tents of Jacob, and the one drawing near <char style="add">with</char> an offering to YHWH of Hosts. <verse eid="MAL 2:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="MAL 2:13"/>And this <char style="add">is</char> the second <char style="add">thing</char> you⁺ do: You cover with tears the altar of YHWH, with weeping and groaning, because there is not anymore turning to the offering or receiving <char style="add">it</char> with acceptance from your⁺ hand. <verse eid="MAL 2:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="MAL 2:14"/>And you⁺ say, “For what?” </para>

<para style="p" vid="MAL 2:14">Because that YHWH is a witness between you and between the wife of your youth, with whom you have dealt treacherously, and she <char style="add">is</char> your companion and the wife of your covenant. <verse eid="MAL 2:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="MAL 2:15"/>And did He not make <char style="add">them</char> one, and a remnant of the Spirit unto him? And what <char style="add">is</char> the one? He was seeking seed of God. Therefore keep guard over your⁺ spirit, and do not deal treacherously with the wife of your youth. <verse eid="MAL 2:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="MAL 2:16"/>“For He hates sending away,” says YHWH the God of Israel, “And he <char style="add">who</char> has covered violence with his garment.”<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">“For I hate divorce,” says YHWH the God of Israel. “And he who divorces his wife covers his garment with violence,”</char></note> Says YHWH of Hosts. You⁺ must keep guard over your⁺ spirit and not act treacherously. <verse eid="MAL 2:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="MAL 2:17"/>You⁺ have wearied YHWH with your⁺ words. And you⁺ say, “In what way have we wearied <char style="add">Him</char>?” </para>

<para style="p" vid="MAL 2:17">By your⁺ saying, “Everyone doing evil <char style="add">is</char> good in the eyes of YHWH, and in them He delights,” or, “Where <char style="add">is</char> the God of justice?” <verse eid="MAL 2:17"/></para>

<chapter eid="MAL 2"/>

<chapter number="3" style="c" sid="MAL 3"/>

<para style="s">I Will Send My Messenger</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="MAL 3:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 7:24–35</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 11:7–19</char></note>“Behold, I am sending My messenger, and he will prepare the way before My face.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Matthew 11:10, Mark 1:2, and Luke 7:27</char></note> And suddenly he will come to His temple—the Lord whom you⁺ are seeking, the Messenger of the covenant, in whom you⁺ delight. Behold, He is coming,” says YHWH of Hosts. <verse eid="MAL 3:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="MAL 3:2"/>And who will be enduring the day of His coming? And who will be standing during His appearing? For He <char style="add">is</char> like the fire of a refiner, and like the soap of those laundering. <verse eid="MAL 3:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="MAL 3:3"/>And He will sit as One refining and purifying silver, and He will purify the sons of Levi, and He will refine them like gold and silver, and they will be unto YHWH ones bringing forward an offering in righteousness. <verse eid="MAL 3:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="MAL 3:4"/>And the offering of Judah and Jerusalem will be pleasing to YHWH, as in the days of old, and as <char style="add">in</char> years former. <verse eid="MAL 3:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="MAL 3:5"/>“And I will come near to you⁺ for the judgment, and I will be a witness making haste against the sorcerers, and against the adulterers, and against those swearing to a lie, and against those oppressing the wage of the hireling, the widow and the fatherless, and against those stretching away a sojourner, and not they do fear me,” says YHWH of Hosts. <verse eid="MAL 3:5"/></para>

<para style="s">Robbing God</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="MAL 3:6"/>“For I, YHWH, do not change; and you⁺, sons of Jacob, have not been consumed. <verse eid="MAL 3:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="MAL 3:7"/>From the days of your⁺ fathers, you⁺ have turned aside from My statutes and have not kept them. Return to Me, and I will return to you⁺,” says YHWH of Hosts. </para>

<para style="p" vid="MAL 3:7">“And you⁺ say, ‘In what way can we return?’ <verse eid="MAL 3:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="MAL 3:8"/>Will a man rob God? Yet you⁺ have robbed Me. </para>

<para style="p" vid="MAL 3:8">And you⁺ say, ‘In what way have we robbed You?’ In the tithe and the contribution. <verse eid="MAL 3:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="MAL 3:9"/>With a curse you⁺ are cursed, and you⁺ are robbing Me—the nation—all of it. <verse eid="MAL 3:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="MAL 3:10"/>Bring all the tithe into the house of treasure, that there may be food in My house. And test Me now in this,” says YHWH of Hosts, “If I will not open for you⁺ the windows of the heavens and pour out for you⁺ blessing until <char style="add">there is</char> no space! <verse eid="MAL 3:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="MAL 3:11"/>And I will rebuke for you⁺ the devourer,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">The devourer</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a name for a crop-destroying pest.</char></note> and it will not destroy for you⁺ the fruit of the ground, and the vine in the field will not be barren for you⁺,” says YHWH of Hosts. <verse eid="MAL 3:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="MAL 3:12"/>“And all the nations will call you⁺ blessed, for you⁺ will be a land of delight,” says YHWH of Hosts. <verse eid="MAL 3:12"/></para>

<para style="s">The Book of Remembrance</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="MAL 3:13"/>“Your⁺ words have been strong against Me,” says YHWH. “And you⁺ say, ‘What have we spoken against You?’ <verse eid="MAL 3:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="MAL 3:14"/>You⁺ have said, ‘To serve God <char style="add">is</char> futile! What gain <char style="add">is</char> that we have kept His charge, that we have walked as mourners before the face of YHWH of Hosts? <verse eid="MAL 3:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="MAL 3:15"/>And now we call blessed the arrogant. Also are raised up those doing wickedness; they even test God and escape.’” <verse eid="MAL 3:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="MAL 3:16"/>Then those who feared YHWH spoke, each man with his neighbor. And YHWH listened and heard, and a book of remembrance was written before Him for those fearing YHWH, and for those esteeming His name. <verse eid="MAL 3:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="MAL 3:17"/>“And they will be unto Me,” says YHWH of Hosts, “On the day when I am making a treasured possession; and I will have compassion on them, as when a man has compassion on his son, the one serving him. <verse eid="MAL 3:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="MAL 3:18"/>And you⁺ will return and see between the righteous one the wicked one, between the one serving God <char style="add">and</char> between the one who does not serve Him.” <verse eid="MAL 3:18"/></para>

<chapter eid="MAL 3"/>

<chapter number="4" style="c" sid="MAL 4"/>

<para style="s">The Day of Yahweh</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="MAL 4:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">2 Peter 3:8–13</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Thessalonians 5:1–11</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Zephaniah 1:7–18</char></note>“For behold, the day is coming, burning like a furnace, and all the proud and all those doing wickedness will be <char style="add">as</char> stubble; and the day that is coming will burn them up,” says YHWH of Hosts, “So that it will not leave for them a root or branch!” <verse eid="MAL 4:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="MAL 4:2"/>“And for you⁺ who fear My name the sun of righteousness will arise, <char style="add">with</char> healing in its wings.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Sun of Righteousness will rise with healing in His wings</char></note> And you⁺ will go forth, and you⁺ will leap like calves from the stall. <verse eid="MAL 4:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="MAL 4:3"/>And you⁺ will trample the wicked, for they will be ashes under the soles of your⁺ feet, on the day that I am preparing,” says YHWH of Hosts. <verse eid="MAL 4:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="MAL 4:4"/>“Remember the Law of Moses My servant that I commanded him on Horeb<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, Mount Sinai, or possibly a mountain in the range containing Mount Sinai</char></note> for all Israel—the statutes and ordinances. <verse eid="MAL 4:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="MAL 4:5"/>Behold, I am sending to you⁺ Elijah the prophet, before the face of the coming of the day of YHWH great and awesome. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">dreadful</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">glorious</char></note><verse eid="MAL 4:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="MAL 4:6"/>And he will turn the heart of the fathers to the sons, and the heart of sons to their fathers,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Luke 1:17</char></note> lest I come and strike the land with a curse.” <verse eid="MAL 4:6"/></para>

<chapter eid="MAL 4"/>

</usx>
